      "writtenOn": "2018-08-15T23:35:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not our style guide (we\u0027re Android), but the Android guide doesn\u0027t say anything specifically about it; however, the telephony code features a few very prominent and persistent cases of this:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/services/Telephony/+/master/src/com/android/phone/PhoneInterfaceManager.java#472\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/master/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ServiceStateTracker.java#2684\n\nSadly, the telephony code is not 100% consistent, but in absence of a closing brace (which also creates some whitespace separation), I feel like it\u0027s done more-often-than-not... your call.",
      "parentUuid": "bdf7d264_11ae5f60",
      "revId": "5d1c37f15db2089d456fce40310e6c8b3f3283da",
