        "id": 1081638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-16T00:20:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android coding guideline says, \"Android follows standard Java coding conventions with the additional rules described below.\" Then the question is, what\u0027s the standard Java coding conventions? Is that the one from Oracle https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/java/codeconventions-150003.pdf? (Page 14)\n\nOr the one from Google?\n\nOracle\u0027s has a space, Google\u0027s does not.",
      "parentUuid": "5746e2d7_a7fb549a",
      "revId": "5d1c37f15db2089d456fce40310e6c8b3f3283da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c453aac_f295a63b",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/data/QualifiedNetworksService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 285,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-15T17:35:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a high-level question, do we expect that multiple system components will register for this? If not, could we register the callbacks at the same time we create one for a slot (and implicitly deregister when we remove one for a slot)?\n\nThere\u0027s 2 parts to that:\n1) if it\u0027s a single-registrant then it\u0027s straightforward.\n2) if it\u0027s a multi-registrant, then the creation/deletion will need to be refcounted so that we don\u0027t have a separate registrant that isn\u0027t aware that the thing is going to be deleted unless we want to provide some sort of onRemoved() notification callback to the other registrants.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 285,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 285,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5d1c37f15db2089d456fce40310e6c8b3f3283da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73205863_9c0813a8",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/data/QualifiedNetworksService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 285,
      "author": {
        "id": 1170206
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-15T18:47:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jack can probably answer better.\n\nSeems to me there might be multiple registrants.\n\nAgree that we don\u0027t have a onRemoved() to the registrants upon deletion of updater, which is true for NetworkService and DataService. We assumed deletion will not really happen, although I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s true. Or another question is upon onRemoved, what registrants should do..? It\u0027s something we can think about later.",
      "parentUuid": "9c453aac_f295a63b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 285,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 285,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5d1c37f15db2089d456fce40310e6c8b3f3283da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
